You are a Senior Frontend Architect, Senior React Engineer, UI/UX Designer, Product Designer, Accessibility Engineer, and Performance Engineer.

Build a production-quality Arabic vocabulary and learning web application called:

LISAN
"Learn Arabic, Grow Closer"

The application must be built using React + TypeScript and should be designed as a scalable real-world product capable of supporting millions of users.

Do NOT create a simple demo.
Do NOT create a generic dashboard.
Do NOT use placeholder-looking UI.
Do NOT use emoji as UI icons.
Do NOT use browser-default styling.

Build a polished, modern, accessible, responsive Arabic learning application.

==================================================
1. PRODUCT VISION
==================================================

Lisan is a free Arabic learning platform focused on:

- Arabic vocabulary
- Arabic pronunciation
- Arabic examples
- Arabic grammar
- Practice
- Quizzes
- Listening
- Flashcards
- Progress tracking
- Bookmarks
- Spaced repetition

The primary learning experience should be extremely simple:

Discover → Learn → Listen → Practice → Review → Track Progress

The application must support:

Arabic
English
Arabic transliteration

Arabic must be displayed correctly using RTL layout.

Arabic vocabulary should preferably contain harakat/tashkeel where appropriate.

Example:

English:
Apple

Arabic:
تُفَّاح

Transliteration:
tuffāḥ


==================================================
2. TECHNOLOGY STACK
==================================================

Use:

- React
- TypeScript
- Vite
- React Router
- CSS Modules OR well-structured global CSS
- TanStack Query
- Zustand OR React Context
- React Hook Form
- Zod
- Vitest
- React Testing Library
- Playwright
- ESLint
- Prettier

Do NOT use unnecessary libraries.

Use reusable components.

Use strongly typed TypeScript.

Avoid:

- any
- duplicated components
- duplicated CSS
- hard-coded repeated values
- giant components
- giant files
- unnecessary state
- prop drilling where inappropriate


